5</italic> and Tn<italic>10</italic>.</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B</source><volume>244</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>9</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Kennedy1"><label>7</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Guhathakurta</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kleckner</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Haniford</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Tn<italic>10</italic> transposition via a DNA hairpin intermediate.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>125</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9778253</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Haniford1"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haniford</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Transposon Tn<italic>10</italic>.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Craig</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Craigie</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gellert</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lambowitz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Mobile DNA II</source><publisher-loc>Washington (D. C.)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>American Society for Microbiology</publisher-name><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>483</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Mizuuchi1"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mizuuchi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Craigie</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Mechanism of bacteriophage Mu transposition.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Genet</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>429</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3028246</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Craigie1"><label>10</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Craigie</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mizuuchi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Mechanism of transposition of bacteriophage Mu: Structure of a transposition intermediate.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>867</fpage><lpage>876</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2988793</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Mizuuchi2"><label>11</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mizuuchi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Transpositional recombination: Mechanistic insights from studies of Mu and other elements.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Biochem</source><volume>61</volume><fpage>1011</fpage><lpage>1051</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1323232</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Chaconas1"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chaconas</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lavoie</surname><given-names>BD</given-names></name><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>DNA transposition: Jumping genes machine, some assembly required.</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>817</fpage><lpage>820</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8805293</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Luria1"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luria</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Delbruck</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1943</year><article-title>Mutations of bacteria from virus sensitivity to virus resistance.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>28</volume><fpage>491</fpage><lpage>511</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17247100</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Berg2"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1983</year><article-title>Structural requirements for IS<italic>50</italic>-mediated gene transposition.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>792</fpage><lpage>796</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6298776</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-York1"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>York</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Welch</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Goryshin</surname><given-names>IY</given-names></name><name><surname>Reznikoff</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Simple and efficient generation in vitro of nested deletions and inversions: Tn<italic>5</italic> intramolecular transposition.</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>1927</fpage><lpage>1933</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9518484</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Sakai1"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sakai</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kleckner</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>The Tn<italic>10</italic> synaptic complex can capture a target DNA only after transposon excision.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>89</volume><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>214</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9108476</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Craig1"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Craig</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>Unity in transposition reactions.</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>270</volume><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>254</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7569973</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Tavakoli1"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tavakoli</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><name><surname>Derbyshire</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Tipping the balance between replicative and simple transposition.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>29</volume><fpage>2923</fpage><lpage>2930</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11387225</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-May1"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>May</surname><given-names>EW</given-names></name><name><surname>Craig</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Switching from cut-and-paste to replicative Tn<italic>7</italic> transposition.</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>272</volume><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>404</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8602527</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pgen.1000619-Saariaho1"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saariaho</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Savilahti</surname><